            <ArticleTitle>Association of platelet count with residual thrombus in the myocardial infarct-related coronary artery among patients treated with fibrinolytic therapy for ST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1406-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A higher platelet count is independently associated with the presence of residual thrombus in the infarct-related artery after administration of fibrinolytic therapy, even after multivariate adjustment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
